# Destination ceiling for org-policy@v12.
#
# Where repository data may be sent. One host, or one host/path prefix, per
# line. A mandate may name these or anything beneath them, and nothing else.
#
# This is a plain list rather than Cedar because Cedar decides
# (principal, action, resource) questions and has no destination in its model;
# expressing it as a policy would mean inventing an entity for it. An empty
# list permits nothing, which is why this file is a required input to
# loadCeiling rather than an optional one.

# The organization's own repositories.
github.com/acme

# The API and git transport hosts the GitHub App token is used against. A bare
# host would also cover every subdomain, so these are named exactly.
api.github.com
codeload.github.com
objects.githubusercontent.com
